## Overview

Grand Theft Auto VI is presented as a single-player experience.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

## Premise

The story follows Jason and Lucia in Vice City, USA, caught in a criminal conspiracy across the state of Leonida.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

## Platform and technical features

PlayStation 5 presentation highlights Tempest 3D Audio support.{{cite:playstation-gta6}} PlayStation 5 presentation highlights fast loading on PS5.{{cite:playstation-gta6}} "The game is not playable on PlayStation 4".{{cite:playstation-gta6}} Digital purchases on PS5 can be downloaded and played on the main console via Console Sharing and Offline Play and on other PS5 consoles when logged in.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}} Xbox Cloud Gaming will stream Grand Theft Auto VI on Xbox One beginning at 1am ET on November 19.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}} Xbox Series S users can pre-install the native Xbox version of Grand Theft Auto VI.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}} Cloud playtime purchases for supported games, including Grand Theft Auto VI, became available starting November 11 in supported markets.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}} "Grand Theft Auto VI must be purchased separately" for Xbox Cloud Gaming and cloud availability varies by market and device.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

## Editions and in-game bonuses

The Ultimate Edition includes exclusive vehicles, weapons, apparel, and chapter-linked bonuses for Jason and Lucia.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}} The Ultimate Edition lists specific bonus items such as the Shitzu Squalo and a '67 Vapid Dominator Buggy with storage at the Paradise Garage.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}} Some Ultimate Edition bonuses reference in-game locations with weapon lockers and secure places to deposit stolen goods.{{cite:gta6-official-site}}

