## Overview

The Ultimate Edition includes Grand Theft Auto VI plus the GTAVI: Ultimate Edition Upgrade.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}} "Ultimate Edition bonuses are threaded across all aspects of Jason and Lucia's story" and new items are uncovered behind each chapter.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}}

## Contents

Rockstar's official list of Ultimate Edition items includes the '95 Grotti Cheetah, Hawk & Little Morgan Revolvers, and Personalized Weapon Variants.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}} The official contents list also names "Jason's Safehouse Vehicles, Ganado Retro Build, Rideout Customs Mod Shop", and Sara's Unisex Salon.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}} Additional listed items include the "Shitzu Squalo, Stock 305 Clothing Store, '67 Vapid Dominator Buggy and Garage", and Electric Fang Tattoo Parlor.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}} Rockstar support states that "The Ultimate Edition also bundles One-Eyed Willie's Mod Shop, Goodtime Gear, PTT Youngin$ Compound, and the Classic Car Collection."{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}}

## Upgrade and availability

Owners of the Standard Edition can purchase the Ultimate Edition Upgrade separately at any time.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}} Physical purchasers receive a download code and can upgrade after redeeming their Standard Edition code, but a physical Ultimate Edition is not available.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}}

## Price and store listings

Take-Two lists the Ultimate Edition price as $99.99.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}} PlayStation Store shows the Ultimate Edition priced at $99.99 on its PS5 listing.{{cite:playstation-gta6}}

