## Overview

Rockstar describes Grand Theft Auto VI as a single-player experience.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}} Digital pre-orders and purchases of Grand Theft Auto VI include the Vintage Vice City Pack and one month of GTA+ when bought before November 20, 2026.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}} Rockstar and retailers list GTA+ as tied to the existing GTA Online service and the GTA+ Games Library for classic Rockstar titles.{{cite:taketwo-preorders}}

## Pre-order and Purchase Details

Digital pre-orders could be pre-loaded starting Tuesday, November 10, 2026, on PlayStation and Xbox at specified local times.{{cite:gta6-support-platforms}} PlayStation Store listings state the digital pre-order includes one free month of GTA+ redeemable on PlayStation accounts.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}} Xbox store listings state customers receive a month of GTA+ with qualifying pre-orders and receive a console pop-up when redeemable.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

## Redemption Windows

PlayStation requires the GTA+ subscription to be claimed by March 31, 2027 on the account used to pre-order.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}} Xbox states the GTA+ month "must be redeemed within 180 days after placing" the pre-order.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

## Platform Notes

PlayStation listings indicate Grand Theft Auto VI supports offline play and is for one player.{{cite:playstation-store-ultimate}} Xbox announcement text repeats that "Grand Theft Auto VI is a single-player experience" and sets the game in Vice City, USA.{{cite:xbox-cloud-gta6}}

